          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c008bb650d6198156a666b386d430716a60f3050",
          "message": "fix(sglang): keep ATOM's attention backend for Qwen4Exp QSA layers on SGLang 0.5.20 (#2427)\n\nSGLang 0.5.20's hybrid-GDN backend wrapper replaces the full-attention\nchild with its own QwenSparseAttnBackend whenever is_qwen_qsa(hf_config)\nholds. For Qwen3.8-Flash-Next served through the ATOM plugin that bypasses\nATOMAttnBackendForSgl, so init_forward_metadata_out_graph never runs,\nprepare_qwen4_exp_decode_graph_metadata never allocates the persistent QSA\npage tables, and CUDA-graph capture dies in _fill_qsa_like_native on\n`assert graph.block_tables is not None` (decode capture without MTP,\ntarget-verify capture with EAGLE MTP; the recipe's own command hits it).\n\nReport \"not QSA\" to SGLang for Qwen4Exp architectures when the ATOM model\npackage serves them, and defer to SGLang otherwise.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
