          "id": "fbb89df0fc2b952923abc76c2206b9012629a401",
          "message": "perf(deepseek_v41): packed FP4 index logits and a two-source BF16 decode (#2513)\n\n* perf(deepseek_v41): packed FP4 index logits and a two-source BF16 decode\n\nPacked index logits (FP4 index plane): the scorer's FP32 logits are no\nlonger a [rows, max_model_len] plane (6-8 GiB at 1M) but one buffer, each\nrow as long as its own visibility, sized from the PAGE pool the memory\nbudget can hold. `ScorePlanner`, a step planner (`add_step_planner`), lays\neach step's rows out band by band; a step whose rows overflow one band\n(requests sharing a prefix the pool stores once) runs eagerly, in bands:\n`AttentionMetadataBuilder.step_needs_eager`, agreed across DP in\n`ForwardMode.decide` (a new `sync_dp_metadata` row). The step planner\nprotocol returns a `StepPlan`: published rows plus what the planner works\nout on the host (`BatchStep.planned_host`).\n\nTwo-source BF16 decode: decode attention reads the selection from the pool\nand the window through the layer's own ring (`ring_view`), one window-row\nlist for every layer and one selection plane per index group, through\n`sparse_attn_v4_paged_2src` (renamed from `sparse_attn_v4_paged_prefill`,\nfile `paged_2src.py`), whose OPUS kernel splits each token's keys when the\nstep has too few tokens to fill the GPU.\n\nNeeds ROCm/aiter#6334 (`top_k_per_row_decode(row_starts=, plane_width=)`,\n`flydsl_pa_mqa_logits_fp4(out_offsets=)`, OPUS split-K).\n\n* refactor(mono): name each launcher's FlyDSL cache directory after its kernel\n\nFlyDSL names a launcher's cache directory after the function, so every\nmono launcher compiled into an anonymous `launch_<hash>`. `launcher(symbol)`\n(next to `kernel_symbol`) jits it and names it `launch_<stem>_<params>`\nafter the kernel's symbol, e.g. `launch_v41_attn_pre_s48_f1_ix0_i41_a0_tl0`.\nIt renames once jitted: FlyDSL's AST rewriter finds the function by its\nname and, on a miss, keeps the source unrewritten.\n\nUsed by the V4.1 mono kernels, the V4.1 router, `step_begin` and the\nMiniMax-M3 mono kernels.\n\n* test(deepseek_v41): check the packed band rule without importing the backend\n\nThe backend pulls triton in, which the CPU unit-test runner lacks; the rule\nis ScoreWorkspace.fits, step_needs_eager only forwards it.",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-10T13:05:33+08:00",
