          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6fd1bb1be97c79b571eb86674786d0d888353b73",
          "message": "[DP] Balance DP-attention prefill steps by estimated chunk cost (#2551)\n\n* [DP] Balance DP-attention prefill steps by estimated chunk cost\n\nUnder DP attention every rank prefills in the same lockstep step, and the\nstep lasts as long as the costliest rank's chunk: the others wait at the MoE\ndispatch of every layer. Ranks fill the same token budget, but a chunk whose\nnew tokens attend a long context costs far more than one after a short one.\n\nWith DP attention over more than one rank, each prefill step is now balanced\nby estimated cost instead of tokens:\n\n- Each rank with prefill work estimates the chunk it would take at the whole\n  batch budget (resumable partials, then the head of waiting, probing the\n  prefix cache without recording and reusing the head's block hashes):\n  cost = k x (W + start + k/2) for k new tokens after start cached ones.\n- The costs ride the PrefillDelayer's existing CPU all_reduce (dp_size more\n  slots, each rank writes its own); no extra collective.\n- Target = min(costliest, mean x (1 + slack)); a rank above it admits fewer\n  tokens this step (never below a floor), and the rest of its prompt\n  continues through the usual chunked-prefill path.\n- Prefill forward labels carry nctx, the attended-context work of the chunk.\n\nKnobs: ATOM_DP_PREFILL_BALANCE_TOKEN_WEIGHT (W, 360000),\nATOM_DP_PREFILL_BALANCE_SLACK (0.1), ATOM_DP_PREFILL_BALANCE_MIN_TOKENS\n(4096). Without DP attention, or with one rank, the scheduler takes the same\npath as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: yihonglie <hyi@amd.com>\n\n* [DP] tests: give test_swa_replay_start's fake scheduler _prefill_room\n\nScheduler._partial_prefill_chunk now takes its budget from _prefill_room (the\nbatch budget, and under DP prefill cost balancing the cost left to the step's\ntarget), so the SimpleNamespace scheduler binds it too, with balancing off\n(_tick_cost_limit = inf), where the room is the batch budget as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: yihonglie <hyi@amd.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: yihonglie <hyi@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
