          "id": "4b3488b34a12e0117a0d3a99020c2625261e1b82",
          "message": "perf(v41): run decoder SWA bounded replay under DP attention (#2569)\n\n* perf(v41): run decoder SWA bounded replay under DP attention\n\nDecoder bounded replay was off whenever DP attention was on: the decoder's\nMoE collectives are sized by every rank's row count, and a rank-local tail\nchanges it. Under DPA every prefill chunk therefore ran all 40 layers, while\nTP runs layers 20-39 only on each finishing prompt's last window rows, which\nmade DPA prefill ~29% slower than TP2 at c128 in InferenceX AgentX.\n\nOn an eager, unsplit DP step the ranks now trade their decoder and last-layer\nrow counts (one CPU all_reduce of 2 x dp_size ints) and size the decoder's\nMoE gathers from that table (dp_rows). A rank finishing no prompt joins each\ncollective on two idle rows under a request-less step, so attention writes\nnothing; a rank that does not replay runs all its rows. TBO-split steps still\ncompute every row.\n\n* refactor(v41): name the DP replay helpers after the token counts they sync\n\ndp_rows_exchangeable -> dp_stage_sync_enabled, exchange_dp_rows ->\nsync_dp_stage_tokens, DPRows -> DPStageTokens (last -> last_layer),\ndp_rows -> dp_token_counts, _idle_decoder -> _join_decoder_collectives.\nThe DP CPU group is looked up through _dp_cpu_group so the unit tests no\nlonger import aiter (the non-GPU test job has none).\n\n* style(v41): sort the bounded_replay imports\n\n* fix(v41): decide DP decoder replay from explicit group flags; cut the image mask for placeholder rows\n\n- Each rank now also reports whether it replays and whether it has decoder\n  work. The group replays when any rank replays, even if every count\n  happens to equal the step's own (a 1-2 row non-final prefill beside a\n  decoding peer used to skip its placeholder pass while the peer ran the\n  decoder, hanging the MoE collectives).\n- When no rank has decoder work (every rank on a non-final chunk), all\n  ranks skip the decoder instead of running placeholder rows through it.\n- The placeholder step (placeholder_rows_of) also cuts the image mask to its\n  rows, so an image prefill with no finishing request does not fail the MoE\n  router's mask-shape check.\n\n* perf(v41): carry the DP replay stage counts in the step's packed DP sync\n\nThe decoder/last-layer token counts were traded in a second CPU all_reduce\ninside every DP prefill forward. Each rank can compute them from its batch\nbefore the step's metadata exists, so they now ride ForwardMode.decide's one\npacked all_gather as four optional rows (sync_dp_metadata stage_tokens),\nreported by the attention builder hook dp_stage_tokens (default None).\n\nsync_dp_metadata returns the table only when some rank replays on a prefill\nstep TBO did not split, so the group decision is made once at the source:\nreplayable and the runtime just read dp_stage_tokens(forward), and the\nduplicated DP/TBO checks (dp_stage_sync_enabled) are gone. The runtime\nchecks that its replay plan runs exactly the counts its rank reported.\n\n* refactor(v41): prepare the DP replay stages with the forward context\n\nThe per-stage DPMetadata is now built once in set_forward_context from the\nstep's DP sync (ForwardContext.dp_stages) and switched by a ForwardContext\nmethod (use_dp_stage). The model no longer constructs DP metadata or writes\ncontext fields mid-forward. Adds a runtime test that placeholder rows run\nlayers 20..38 under the decoder counts and layer 39 under the last-layer\ncounts.\n\n* test(v41): skip the runtime stage test where aiter is absent\n\n* refactor(v41): join the DP decoder collectives on one placeholder row\n\nA rank with no decoder work of its own joins its peers' MoE collectives on\nits first row. Drops DP_PLACEHOLDER_TOKENS and the helper around it; one\nrow runs through the compiled decoder layers without recompiling (checked\non MI355X DPA: no recompiles, gsm8k 0.9204 / 0.9219).\n\n* refactor(v41): one replay decision, generic DP stage sync, CPU-run invariants\n\nReview follow-ups (PR 2569):\n- One decision: a DP rank decides from its batch (replays_batch), reports\n  it with its counts, and replayable() acts on that report\n  (ForwardContext.dp_stages.applies) instead of re-deriving it.\n- Shared layers carry no V4.1 semantics: the builder hook returns a\n  DPStageReport (stage names and counts, applies, active), the packed sync\n  carries a variable-length row and reads only its applies flag, and the\n  forward context builds one DPMetadata per named stage.\n- Every decoder path (full rows, tail, placeholder) runs through\n  run_decoder_stages; its stage mapping and the report/plan agreement are\n  tested on CPU, so CI runs them.\n- Drop DPStageTokens (only decoder_active was read) and the name reused\n  for three things; skip host work on non-replaying steps; restore the\n  scalar min in build_replay_plan.\n- Docs and the startup log describe DP replay and the placeholder row.\n\n* test(v41): run the report/plan agreement test without Triton\n\n* refactor(v41): name the DP stage types after bounded replay\n\nDPStageReport -> BoundedReplayDPReport, DPStage -> BoundedReplayDPStage,\nDPStages -> BoundedReplayDPStages, _dp_stages -> _bounded_replay_dp_stages.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ZhangLirong-amd <219599949+ZhangLirong-amd@users.noreply.github.com>",
