          "id": "23545f5281ce6cd0e126a470eb32b0a5a41652a2",
          "message": "[Scheduler] #2588 follow-ups: stop the cold prefix walk at its first miss, ship prompt chains beside the seqs (#2599)\n\n* Stub aiter only while test_io_processor_fanout imports the engine\n\nThe file put a fake `atom.model_engine.engine_core_mgr` into `sys.modules`\nat collection and never removed it, so every test file collected with it\nimported the stub: test_admission_host_overhead failed in either order and\nunder -k. Import `llm_engine` under `stubbed_aiter()` instead, which drops\nits fake modules on exit.\n\n* Rename ATOM_PREFILL_DELAYER_PROBE_MEMO to ATOM_PREFIX_WALK_MEMO\n\nThe memo serves every per-tick probe of a waiting request, the DP\nchunk-cost estimate as well as the delayer, so the name should not tie it\nto the delayer. New in this PR, so no alias.\n\n* Stop the cold prefix walk at its first miss; tighten the index invariants\n\n- `_hit_walk` looked the whole adopted prompt chain up in its first round,\n  so a cold 186k-token probe cost ~0.35 ms instead of ~2 us. Look the\n  first block up alone, then rounds of 16, 64, ... blocks: lookups stay\n  within ~4x the hit.\n- `_can_admit_head_prefill` runs every tick on DP>1 and still called the\n  exact probe; use `can_allocate_memoized` like the other per-tick probes.\n- `BlockPool.publish` revokes a different hash the block was still indexed\n  under, as an eviction does (event, state unindex, memo invalidation):\n  the fast walk's last-block compare relies on indexed content never\n  changing. No current path publishes over an indexed hash.\n- `index_version` moves only when a hash leaves the index or moves to\n  another id, so a republish in place or a new hash no longer forces\n  `allocate` to revalidate the ids it claims.\n- `_chain_to` checks that the hashes it continues are a prefix of the\n  prompt chain (first and last overlapping link) and hashes past them\n  otherwise.\n\n* Ship prompt chains beside the seqs in the ADD frame, never inside them\n\n`prompt_hash_chain` was pickled with its Sequence, so four places had to\nclear it by hand. Now `Sequence.__getstate__` drops it, the frontend\ndetaches the chains into the ADD frame's third element\n(`take_shipped_chains`, which also frees the frontend's copy) and the\nengine's input thread hands them back (`attach_shipped_chains`). The\nDisaggCoreManager prefill engine has no BlockManager, so its copy goes\nwithout; decode, which allocates, gets them. Frames without chains keep\ntheir two-element shape.\n\nThe order-dependent test now imports the engine modules for real even if\nanother file left a stub in `sys.modules`, and follows the frame from\n`CoreManager.add_request` through `EngineCore.process_input_sockets`.\n\n* Docs: allocate no longer compares tokens; the walk rounds and the ADD frame\n\n- scheduling_kv_cache_guide: `allocate` claims the walk's ids (revalidated\n  only if the index moved) and compares no tokens; `publish` revokes a\n  block's old hash; the memo serves the delayer's head check too.\n- environment_variables: the walk memo row moves next to the other two\n  prefix-lookup switches and names every per-tick probe; the fast walk's\n  lookup rounds; where the shipped chain travels.",
