          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2344f1739379be9a459a2bc82f05953f7e44b213",
          "message": "fix(atomesh-ci): TW Spur weekly failures (Mesh cache, PENDING dispatch, amd-tw account) (#2625)\n\n* fix(atomesh-ci): pass Spur scheduler results as attached options\n\nCancelled and timed-out Spur jobs report exit code \"-1:0\". argparse read\nthat value as an option and pd_job_result.py exited with \"expected one\nargument\", so the job result was never recorded and the cell failed with\nrc=2 instead of the scheduler's result.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(atomesh-ci): wait for Spur to report RUNNING before dispatching workers\n\nSpur can start the batch script while its controller still reports the\njob as PENDING. srun then fails with \"job is not running (state: Pending)\"\nand no worker starts (job 8793, plus at least eight earlier jobs). Poll\nscontrol before exec srun, waiting only on an explicit PENDING/CONFIGURING\nstate for up to ATOMESH_SPUR_RUNNING_TIMEOUT (300s); an unavailable\ncontroller dispatches immediately as before.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(atomesh-ci): cancel Spur jobs that run without starting workers\n\nJob 8793 stayed RUNNING for its full 8h limit after its batch script\nfailed to dispatch, with no rank output at all. monitor_slurm_job now\ntakes an optional SLURM_STARTUP_PROGRESS_CHECK; pd_submit.sh enables it\nfor Spur and cancels a job that has been RUNNING for\nATOMESH_SPUR_STARTUP_TIMEOUT (900s) without any rank-workload-* or\nrank-rc-* file.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(atomesh-ci): keep the Mesh Cargo cache out of /tmp\n\nThe Spur epilog runs 'find /tmp /var/tmp ... -user $UID -type f -mtime +1\n-delete' when the CI user has no other job on the node. Cargo stamps\nextracted crate sources with a 2006 mtime, so every source file went at\nthe next epilog while the fresh .cargo-ok markers stayed, and Cargo then\nrefused to re-extract: on pit2-p03-g12 all 477 crates lost Cargo.toml and\nevery Mesh build failed with 'failed to read .../Cargo.toml' (jobs 8782,\n8838).\n\nDefault ATOMESH_MESH_TARGET_DIR to <log root>/.mesh-cache/<host>-<uid>\non the shared log storage, one directory per host so nodes do not\ncontend for each other's build lock.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(atomesh-ci): submit TW Spur cells as amd-atom/amd-atom-qos\n\npit2-vm-amd-xl-02 rewrote the partition and QOS but kept the matrix\naccount. The weekly GLM-5.2 cells carry account amd-tw, which the CI user\nis not associated with on Spur, so all 14 were rejected at sbatch:\n\"user 'junyan.yang@amd.com' is not associated with account 'amd-tw'\".\nRewrite the account too: -A amd-atom --qos=amd-atom-qos -p amd-spur.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(atomesh-ci): drop retired TW account and partition choices\n\namd-tw is not an account the CI user can submit to on Spur, and TW cells\nnow run on the amd-spur partition, so remove amd-tw from the account\nchoices and amd-frameworks/amd-tw from the partition choices.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(atomesh-ci): describe the QOS for each Slurm account choice\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* style: black-format the Mesh cache default test\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: junyan.yang@amd.com <junyan.yang@amd.com@pit2-vm-amd-xl-02.amd.pit2.tensorwave.lan>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
