          "id": "89e4e3147a7e40f315ddae48a02c544d5fddde3e",
          "message": "feat(mhc): use HIP Mega-MHC by default for supported DeepSeek V4.1 (#2568)\n\n* feat(mhc): integrate HIP Mega-MHC for DeepSeek V4.1\n\n* test(mhc): remove standalone HIP integration tests\n\n* feat(mhc): fuse quantization before DeepSeek V4.1 attention\n\nReuse HIP Mega-MHC MXFP8 output for QKV projection while retaining\nBF16 hidden states for the compressor and indexer.\n\nCarry quantized inputs through compiled execution, DSpark and bounded\nreplay. Enable fusion whenever attention selects HIP; keep FFN BF16.\n\nExtend compilation tests to cover fused outputs and optional inputs.\n\n* fix(vllm): support fused quantization in V4.1 attention\n\nPass the optional fused FP8 hidden tensor through the capture-break\nattention copy and reuse it for QKV projection. Keep BF16 hidden for\nauxiliary readers and the attention output buffer.\n\nRefresh the core-forward digest after syncing the copy and add CPU\nregressions for fused/plain inputs and bounded-query forwarding.",
