          "id": "e3a00a9281ee0ce84a3cc0129fac28a974b17c9b",
          "message": "fix(sglang): match the mono-refusal stand-in to the signature it replaces (#2705)\n\n`install_minimax_mono_plugin_refusal` rebinds\n`minimax_m3.mono.dispatch._config_refusal` so SGLang refuses mono before the\nTR_HYBRID cudagraph clause can read a `cudagraph_mode` it never sets.\n\n#2479 folded the `use_index_cache` clause into `common_refusals` and dropped\n`text_config` from the native signature and its one call site, but left the\nstand-in taking `(atom_config, text_config)`. `MonoDecode.__init__` passes\none argument, so every SGLang MiniMax-M3 launch raised\n\n    TypeError: install_minimax_mono_plugin_refusal.<locals>._config_refusal()\n               missing 1 required positional argument: 'text_config'\n\nat model construction, failing the `ci:sglang` accuracy job for any PR that\ntriggered it.\n\nA rebind is invisible to ruff and black -- they see two unrelated functions --\nand the only code path that exercises the pairing is an SGLang MiniMax-M3\nlaunch, which runs in the heavy job rather than pre-checkin. So the pairing is\npinned by a test that reads both definitions with `ast`: no import, hence no\n`importorskip`, hence it actually runs on the CPU-only runner where the drift\nwould otherwise go unnoticed again. A second case pins the native signature\nagainst its call site, so a future change has to move all three together.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
