          "id": "f324de48a444e9b6edf3603b126c079608ad3f7d",
          "message": "[gfx1250] DeepSeek-V4.1: run on gfx1250 (MI455X) with FlyDSL kernels (#2617)\n\n* [gfx1250] DeepSeek-V4.1: run on gfx1250 (MI455X) with FlyDSL kernels\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash now starts and serves on gfx1250 at TP4 and DEP4, with\nits FP8 linears and index scoring on AITER's FlyDSL kernels. Requires AITER\n#6863 (FlyDSL paged FP8 MQA logits, merged) and #6864 (FlyDSL batched\nmxfp8_32 GEMM with 32x32 weight scales and K tails).\n\nRun on gfx1250:\n- Mono decode's persistent kernels are gfx950 code (wave64, MFMA,\n  permlane32) and fail to compile on gfx1250. Mono's shared deployment checks\n  now refuse any arch but gfx950, so V4.1 (and DSpark's draft and verify)\n  take the unfused path there. The arch is read on use through\n  `deployment._gfx()`, so the module still imports without `aiter.jit`; tests\n  pin it to gfx950 (autouse fixture) and one test patches it back.\n- The fixed-order router GEMV is the same gfx950 bf16 MFMA tile and fails to\n  compile on gfx1250; `router_supported` is gfx950-only, elsewhere the gate's\n  own GEMM routes.\n\nFlyDSL kernels on gfx1250:\n- Every FP8 linear with 32x32 weight scales (wqkv_a, wq_b, wo_b, the indexer's\n  wq_b, DSpark's main_proj, Engram's wkv) and the grouped wo_a run on the\n  FlyDSL mxfp8_32 GEMM, which reads the 32x32 scale as stored; a K that 128\n  does not divide (the shared expert's down projection, K = 576 at TP4) runs\n  as a ragged last k-tile.\n- FP8 index scoring (`indexer/score.py`) uses `flydsl_fp8_paged_mqa_logits`\n  on gfx1250, over the same packed, preshuffled 8-row-page cache and with the\n  same arguments as the Triton kernel. This is the shared paged scorer, so\n  any model using it on gfx1250 takes the FlyDSL kernel; other archs are\n  unchanged.\n\nEngram under DP attention (DEP4):\n- With DP attention every rank's TP group is one GPU, so each rank registers\n  its Engram tables whole, and DEP4 needed ATOM_ENGRAM_UVA=0. A layer's\n  scales sit right before its values in the shard; each range is widened to\n  page boundaries for cudaHostRegister, so the two share a page and HIP\n  refuses the overlapping registration. Registration now goes through a\n  process-wide, reference-counted set of page-locked runs (a shared page is\n  registered once, released with its last user), and a refused registration\n  clears HIP's last error instead of failing the next kernel launch.\n- safe_open maps a shard privately, so page-locking copied every table page\n  into each DP rank. Tables are now read through a shared, read-only mapping\n  of the shard, so registration pins the same page-cache pages for every\n  rank. The TP path (each rank registers its head shard) is unchanged.\n\nDocs: recipes/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.md gains a gfx1250 (MI455X) section with\nTP4 / DEP4 launch commands, the differences from gfx950 and GSM8K results.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(observability): allow additional runner startup RPCs\n\n(cherry picked from commit 99908e19b482f104d850419bd6d0083374564c91)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: NidhoggD1 <nidhoggd1@gmail.com>",
