          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d1c7bb245e55921d79e9dde5f498cfd41d55cd0a",
          "message": "refactor: shared DSA indexer forward and top-k schedule, sparse prefill decided once, DCP kernel cleanup (#2776)\n\n* refactor: shared DSA indexer forward and top-k schedule, sparse prefill decided once, DCP kernel cleanup\n\nStructure\n- The model registry (support_model_arch_dict, mono_decode_installers) moves\n  from model_runner.py to atom/models/registry.py.\n- The DSA indexer op (sparse_attn_indexer) moves from models/deepseek_v2.py to\n  model_ops/indexer/indexer_forward.py.\n- model_ops/indexer/schedule.py is the one classification of which layers\n  reuse an earlier layer's top-k; the model, the MLA layer and the PP runner\n  all read it.\n- The MLA metadata builder decides sparse prefill once a step\n  (attn_metadata.run_sparse); MLA, the indexer, PCP and the sglang bridge\n  follow it.\n- flatten_dsa_config publishes a nested dsa_config as the flat index_* fields;\n  index planes are allocated only for the layers it names.\n- GDN causal-conv metadata is built from host-side sequence lengths.\n- atom.model_ops.indexer loads its names on first use, so its kernel-free\n  submodules import without AITER.\n- Kimi-K3 image request inputs move to atom/models/kimi_k3/image_processing.py,\n  so building them does not import the vision model or AITER.\n\nIndexer and sparse MLA\n- NoPE indexer: index_rope_dim, a fused FP8 query-quant and key-cache writer\n  (model_ops/indexer/nope.py), and keys/head weights projected by the owning\n  attention; the unpooled glm5_next path uses the shared indexer.\n- A single-rank FP8 prefill subtracts request bases inside the slot\n  conversion instead of rewriting the top-k tensor.\n- Sparse-prefill work buffers are sized for prefill's own gathered head\n  width; a BF16 sparse-prefill row stays in one work unit, so its result does\n  not depend on batch composition; small BF16 persistent DCP prefills split\n  128 heads into two groups with one shared buffer set bound by the builder.\n- BF16 ASM prefill pads 17..127 query heads to the 128 the kernel accepts.\n- Stable top-k whenever tensor parallelism is on.\n\nDCP\n- The prefill query gather fuses rank-to-token reordering with head padding.\n- zero_nonfinite_rows checks 32 rows per program; the prefill indptr prefix\n  sum is one launch; the decode candidate exchange uses the custom\n  all-gather; ownership and slot mapping are shared helpers.\n- The local logits width covers partial interleave groups, and the prefill\n  key gather ignores padded block-table rows.\n\nLoading\n- A layer the checkpoint stores in a plain float dtype is treated as\n  unquantized, decided from the safetensors headers.\n- Loading warns when a checkpoint float tensor is converted to another float\n  dtype.\n\nKimi-K3\n- KDA control parameters, short convolutions and the output norm are FP32;\n  e_score_correction_bias is FP32.\n- When the config names DSA layers, those layers fuse the indexer key and\n  head-weight projections into the q_a/kv_a projection\n  (K3FusedIndexerProjection).\n- The BF16 output gate uses the fused sigmoid-mul; BF16 gated norm and\n  attention residual keep one reduction layout at every batch size.\n- Vision projections run on the aiter BF16 GEMM.\n\nOther\n- MoE: pure tensor parallelism routes pad rows like real rows for now; a -1\n  route faults the TP a16w4 MoE path.\n- The multimodal chat endpoint returns prompt_token_ids when requested.\n\n* test: stub aiter_mla's new imports in the LMCache MP builder test\n\nThe test loads aiter_mla.py with each import replaced; the head-group and\ntop-k schedule modules it now imports had no stand-in, so the real ones were\nloaded under the stubbed triton and failed.\n\n* fix: run the BF16 sigmoid gate as a custom op under torch.compile\n\nfused_sigmoid_mul_maybe_quant(quant=False) called AITER's\nfused_sigmoid_mul directly. Traced by Dynamo, that wrapper's shape checks\nand mask choice fixed the token count to the one seen while compiling, so\na compiled Kimi-K3 broke its graph at the MLA layer and the following\nlayer frame failed with a ConstraintViolationError on hidden_states.\n\nThe BF16 path is now the guarded op sigmoid_mul, like the FP8 group-quant\npath: its layout checks run at call time and the graph holds one opaque\nnode. Numerics and the out-of-place contract are unchanged.",
